  "figures": [
    {
      "caption": "Post-outcome operating-range diagnostic of the unchanged frozen visual-goal controllers, conducted after the unsuccessful 6\u201312-action hard-goal primary. All six goal-distance shells and all three existing model seeds were admitted before the follow-up. Every point is exact goal hits out of 128 starts before native death or the 24-action limit; whiskers are Wilson 95% intervals for that model and shell only. The same 128 valid prefixes are reused across shells, so neither shells nor model-seed results are pooled into an IID binomial interval. JEPA receives RGB history, outgoing actions and an RGB goal. The H1/H3 controllers retain exhaustive latent-distance search and the H3 summed stage cost; the state oracle uses privileged physical coordinates. The follow-up changes goal distance only and does not replace the original harder-goal result or establish long-horizon planning.",
